Policy: this token has no random-number generator (module README). From
pkcs11-check 0.2.3 (https://github.com/mingulov/pkcs11-check), MIT OR
Apache-2.0, applied to the installed package. Tests that only need random
data (IVs, nonces, payloads) take it through this one helper; when the token
answers CKR_RANDOM_NO_RNG the helper returns host random bytes instead of
failing. Tests of the generator itself either call C_GenerateRandom directly
(unaffected) or go through this helper and then pass on host bytes; those are
kept off the include-list (baseline.txt, tag rng).

--- a/pkcs11_check/raw/recipes.py
+++ b/pkcs11_check/raw/recipes.py
@@ -1521,6 +1521,8 @@
     """Generate random bytes using C_GenerateRandom."""
     buf = (ctypes.c_ubyte * length)()
     rv = raw.C_GenerateRandom(session, buf, length)
+    if rv == 0x121:  # CKR_RANDOM_NO_RNG: the token has no generator, take host bytes
+        return os.urandom(length)
     expect_rv(rv, CKR_OK)
     return bytes(buf)
 
